{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion commands and perception of obstacles. The specification automata enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: the robot advances forward or random_walk when clear, makes brief direction changes for coverage, and uses conservative recovery (short turns or rare backward motion) only when obstacles are detected. full_rotate is reserved for last-resort recovery after repeated failures. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to modularize sensing and actuation.",
    "Specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe, progress-maximizing actions and enforce conservative, non-oscillatory recovery with rapid return to exploration."
  ],
